        "original_id": "544661ee-240b-58ae-8ab6-775d8c2d14d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Miško Jovanović, Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria\n- Places: Bosnia, Austria-Hungary, Hungary, Bohemia\n- Events: Assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand\n- Roles: Archduke, heir presumptive\n\nFacts:\n- Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria was born on 18 December 1863 as Franz Ferdinand Carl Ludwig Joseph Maria.\n- From 1896 until his death, Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria was heir presumptive to the Austro-Hungarian throne.\n- Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria was an Archduke of Austria-Este and a royal prince of Hungary and of Bohemia.\n- Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria died on 28 June 1914.\n- Miško Jovanović, also called Mihajlo \"Miško\" Jovanović, was a Bosnian Serb involved in the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria.\n- Miško Jovanović died on 3 February 1915.",
